0085:     - Each tile region contains one solid non-frame interior block.
0086:     - The unique most common interior color is the default; every other interior color marks four rectangle corners.
0087: 
0088:     Rule
0089:     - For each marker color, find its two row bands and two column bands.
0090:     - Paint that color through background cells along the two horizontal and two vertical sides of the implied rectangle.
0091:     - Preserve all original frame, default interior, marker, and off-path background pixels.
0092: 
0093:     Key insight
0094:     - The repeated tile frames define which cells are obstacles and which cells are background channels; matching interior colors supply rectangle corners independent of tile and marker size.
0095:     """
